<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="office-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="office-title">Costs worth a closer look in an office</h2>
      <dl class="fit-list">
        <div><dt>Rent and deposits</dt><dd>TDS may apply above limits. Deposits are not an expense. Keep the agreement.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Registered office proof</dt><dd>GST and company filings rely on it. Keep your landlord's permission and documents current.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Co-working or virtual offices</dt><dd>Check that the arrangement satisfies GST address requirements before relying on it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Staff and reimbursements</dt><dd>Keep claims and travel records, as these grow quickly.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Making remote accounting work</h2>
      <ol class="mini-steps test-steps">
        <li>Keep invoices and bills in one shared folder, owned by you</li>
        <li>Give named logins for accounting software</li>
        <li>Set a fixed monthly date for documents and queries</li>
        <li>Meet by call monthly, and in person quarterly if you prefer</li>
        <li>Use read-only bank access, or send statements</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="areas-title">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2 id="areas-title" class="first-h2">Areas we are often asked about</h2>
    <p>Delhi's planned commercial structure includes district centres. {% ext "https://realtynmore.com/?p=31226", "A report on DDA plans" %} names centres such as Saket, Netaji Subhash Place, Laxmi Nagar, Rajendra Place, Janakpuri and Nehru Place. Others, like Connaught Place and the Rohini and Pitampura area, are also busy with offices and practices.</p>
    <p>We looked at each of these and did not find enough difference in accounting needs to justify a page for each. What your business does matters more, so we have put the information here.</p>
    <h3 id="nehru-place">Nehru Place is a partial exception</h3>
    <p>Trade press describes it as a major IT hardware market, with bodies such as the All Delhi Computer Traders Association. Traders there resemble {% routeLink "/industries/accounting-for-traders/", "wholesale traders" %} more than offices do: high volume, low margin, serial-numbered stock and warranty claims.</p>
    <p>AccountOrbit has no office in any of these places, and being named here does not mean a professional is based there.</p>
